    <briefdescription>
<para>32-bit Thumb instructions are stored as two little-endian halfwords. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>An instruction at address A encodes bytes A+1, A in the first halfword (Hi), followed by bytes A+3, A+2 in the second halfword (Lo). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
